    "body": "### Problem\n\nThe built-in tmux clipboard provider can block Nvim when pasting from the clipboard register.\n\nAfter copying once in Nvim, quitting, and opening Nvim again, pressing `p` blocks the UI until I press `<C-C>`. This happens only inside tmux.\n\n`tmux refresh-client -l` asks the attached terminal for clipboard contents via an OSC 52 query. In my terminal setup the query does not complete promptly, so the synchronous clipboard read performed by p blocks Nvim.\n\nThis appears to be a regression/compatibility issue introduced by #36787, which intentionally added refresh-client -l to solve the stale clipboard problem from #36786.\n\n**Workaround**\n\nThe issue disappears when I override the tmux provider to read only tmux's local paste buffer:\n```\nif vim.env.TMUX and vim.env.TMUX ~= \"\" then\n  vim.g.clipboard = {\n    name = \"tmux-local-buffer\",\n    copy = {\n      [\"+\"] = { \"tmux\", \"load-buffer\", \"-w\", \"-\" },\n      [\"*\"] = { \"tmux\", \"load-buffer\", \"-w\", \"-\" },\n    },\n    paste = {\n      [\"+\"] = { \"tmux\", \"save-buffer\", \"-\" },\n      [\"*\"] = { \"tmux\", \"save-buffer\", \"-\" },\n    },\n    cache_enabled = 1,\n  }\nend\nvim.o.clipboard = \"unnamedplus\"\n```\nThis avoids the block, but deliberately stops p from importing text copied outside tmux from the outer system clipboard.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nRun this from an SSH session:\n\nInside the first Nvim instance:\n```\ntmux new -s nvim-clipboard-repro\nprintf 'clipboard reproduction\\n' >/tmp/nvim-clipboard-repro.txt\nnvim --clean '+set clipboard=unnamedplus' /tmp/nvim-clipboard-repro.txt\n```\nPress yy\nRun :q\nThen start a fresh instance:\n```\nnvim --clean '+set clipboard=unnamedplus' /tmp/nvim-clipboard-repro.txt\n```\nPress p\n\n### Expected behavior\n\np should return promptly. If the outer terminal does not support or permit OSC 52 clipboard reads, Nvim should not block indefinitely waiting for the tmux clipboard query. A bounded fallback to the existing tmux paste buffer, an asynchronous query, or making the external clipboard refresh opt-in would avoid blocking normal paste operations.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNvim v0.12.4, installed via Snap (Snap Nvim published date is 19 Aug, which I believe is the date this issue was first raised.)\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nno\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nUbuntu 24.04.4 LTS\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nSSH: $TERM=xterm-ghostty\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-ghostty\n\n### Installation\n\nsnap",
